From: Raven Contributors <raven@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Handle numerical zero-flow geometry in KLT verification

Exact stationary GPU tracks do not constrain a fundamental matrix. Verify
those correspondences with a homography without imposing an inertial
stationary update. Keep normal-motion fundamental-matrix verification and
exclude invalid LK tracks from geometric fitting.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Raven Contributors <raven@localhost>

--- a/ov_core/src/track/TrackKLT.cpp
+++ b/ov_core/src/track/TrackKLT.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 
 #include "TrackKLT.h"
 
+#include <cmath>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <optional>
 #include <opencv2/core/ocl.hpp>
@@ -945,25 +946,41 @@
                             cv::OPTFLOW_USE_INITIAL_FLOW);
   }
 
-  // Normalize these points, so we can then do ransac
